1
00:02:36,766 --> 00:02:39,900
<v Teacher> Good afternoon. May I speak to Emma’s parent?

2
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:43,988
<v Father>Afternoon. I’m her father. Who am I speaking to?

3
00:02:43,988 --> 00:02:48,342
<v Teacher> This is Emma’s teacher Jane Carson calling from the Art Centre.

4
00:02:48,342 --> 00:02:51,896
<v Teacher>I’m just calling to talk about her drama class at the centre.


5
00:02:51,896 --> 00:02:56,318
<v Father>Oh, thank you for calling. How’s Emma doing in drama class?

6
00:02:56,318 --> 00:03:04,048
<v Father>You know she just transferred here last month, unlike the others in her class who have been taking the course the whole semester since June.

7
00:03:04,048 --> 00:03:07,591
<v Father>So I’m a bit worried that she might not fit in so well.


8
00:03:07,591 --> 00:03:12,900
<v Teacher>There’s no need to worry. She exhibits a strong performance in her drama class.

9
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:14,205
<v Father>Is that so?

10
00:03:14,205 --> 00:03:23,106
<v Teacher>Yes. She didn’t adapt to the new environment as quickly as I originally expected, and seemed a bit shy at first.

11
00:03:23,096 --> 00:03:30,302
<v Teacher>But a few days later, she made a couple of friends and became more talkative and also more involved in class.

12
00:03:30,302 --> 00:03:37,207
<v Teacher>Emma really is a role model for others, because she has always been an active participant
during class.


13
00:03:37,207 --> 00:03:40,491
<v Teacher>She voices her own ideas and is very creative.

14
00:03:40,491 --> 00:03:45,621
<v Father>I didn’t expect that. But I can tell that she really enjoys the course,

15
00:03:45,621 --> 00:03:49,409
<v Father>because she’s been talking about it at home frequently these past few weeks.


16
00:03:49,409 --> 00:03:53,352
<v Teacher>That’s great to hear. Interest is always the best teacher.

17
00:03:53,352 --> 00:03:59,895
<v Teacher>I also have to inform you that there’s been an adjustment in the timetable of the drama class next term.


18
00:03:59,895 --> 00:04:00,777
<v Father>Why is that?

19
00:04:00,777 --> 00:04:05,881
<v Teacher>It’s not that the music room that we currently use isn’t available.

20
00:04:05,881 --> 00:04:14,168
<v Teacher>As there are too many enrolling for the coming semester, increased class size means that space is limited to house the whole class.

21
00:04:14,168 --> 00:04:23,124
<v Teacher>Also the new classroom we use is not available during the current timeframe, so I’m afraid we have to change the time for it.

22
00:04:23,124 --> 00:04:25,882
<v Father>I see. So when would it be?

23
00:04:25,882 --> 00:04:29,793
<v Teacher> As you know, the current class begins at three fifteen.

24
00:04:29,793 --> 00:04:33,632
<v Teacher>But the new time of thedrama class would be a quarter to five.


25
00:04:33,632 --> 00:04:36,877
<v Father>I’m afraid I have errands to run during that time.

26
00:04:36,877 --> 00:04:45,549
<v Teacher>On the other campus the class still begins at three fifteen, but for the campus Emma goes to, it is the only time available for drama class.

27
00:04:45,549 --> 00:04:51,119
<v Father>Oh. I see. I have to make adjustments to my chore schedule then. No problem.


28
00:05:28,590 --> 00:05:32,746
<v Father>Miss Carson, I’m thinking about signing Emma up for another art course.

29
00:05:32,746 --> 00:05:34,551
<v Father>I’m thinking about dance class.


30
00:05:34,551 --> 00:05:40,741
<v Teacher>Dance class is a popular course here, a great choice for a child to shape up and have fun.

31
00:05:40,741 --> 00:05:44,556
<v Teacher>But unfortunately, it is over-subscribed at the moment.

32
00:05:44,546 --> 00:05:46,593
<v Teacher>I have to put you on the waiting list.

33
00:05:46,593 --> 00:05:50,982
<v Father>That’s too bad. What else can I choose from then? Could you give me some advice?


34
00:05:50,982 --> 00:05:56,897
<v Teacher>Sure. Emma could take singing class as well. This would improve her musicality.

35
00:05:56,887 --> 00:05:58,985
<v Father>Sounds good. When is that?

36
00:05:58,985 --> 00:06:01,870
<v Teacher> It is held every Friday evening.

37
00:06:01,870 --> 00:06:03,095
<v Father>That’s too bad.

38
00:06:03,085 --> 00:06:06,287
 <v Father>Emma already has a swimming class earlier that evening.

39
00:06:06,287 --> 00:06:09,769
<v Father>It will be too late for her to come home if she takes this course.

40
00:06:09,769 --> 00:06:12,417
<v Teacher>There is also a vocal course available. 

41
00:06:12,417 --> 00:06:16,233
<v Teacher>Emma’s got a great voice, I’m sure she’ll stand out in the class.


42
00:06:16,233 --> 00:06:17,415
<v Father>Tell me about it.

43
00:06:17,415 --> 00:06:21,705
<v Teacher>The vocal course starts at 4.30 pm every Tuesday.

44
00:06:21,705 --> 00:06:27,455
<v Teacher>It isn’t fully booked yet. Great teacher, experienced and beloved by students.

45
00:06:27,455 --> 00:06:29,400
<v Teacher>The price is a bit higher though.


46
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:30,397
<v Father>How much is it?

47
00:06:30,397 --> 00:06:32,267
<v Teacher>It’s 110 dollars.

48
00:06:32,267 --> 00:06:35,952
<v Father>Oh, that’s too much, way over our budget.

49
00:06:35,952 --> 00:06:38,603
<v Father>We have to cover the extra cost if we choose it.


50
00:06:38,603 --> 00:06:41,705
<v Teacher> Or maybe Emma could take music class.


51
00:06:41,705 --> 00:06:46,280
<v Father>What is it about? Learning about songs and musicals?


52
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:52,627
<v Teacher> Well, the students have the opportunity to play different instruments like the piano, drum and so on. 

53
00:06:52,627 --> 00:06:56,548
<v Teacher>They can also learn how to write music under professional guidance.

54
00:06:56,548 --> 00:07:00,736
<v Father>That’s exactly what Emma is eager to learn. How much would it cost?

55
00:07:00,736 --> 00:07:03,581
<v Teacher>It was 63 dollars last term.

56
00:07:03,581 --> 00:07:08,413
<v Teacher>But this term it is 85 dollars, 22 dollars more than the original price.

57
00:07:08,413 --> 00:07:11,508
<v Father>We can afford that. When does the course begin?

58
00:07:11,498 --> 00:07:14,035
<v Teacher>The course starts on September 7th.

59
00:07:14,035 --> 00:07:17,826
<v Father>Can we start one week later, on September 14th?

60
00:07:17,826 --> 00:07:21,226
<v Father>My daughter will be on a trip to France with her Mom on the 7th.


61
00:07:21,226 --> 00:07:25,366
<v Teacher>No problem. And the teacher for the class is Jamal Curtis.

62
00:07:25,366 --> 00:07:29,529
<v Teacher>Just contact him if you have any further questions regarding the course.

63
00:07:29,529 --> 00:07:32,561
<v Father>Jamal Curtis? How do you spell Curtis?

64
00:07:32,561 --> 00:07:37,395
<v Teacher> Oh, it’s C-U-R-T-I-S.

65
00:07:37,395 --> 00:07:38,046
<v Father>Thank you.